WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.630 --> 00:00:03.060
SPEAKER 1: Benjamin is
now the favored son.

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:05.250
You other brothers
go, because there

00:00:05.250 --> 00:00:06.960
could be some harm on the way.

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:09.540
But don't let me
lose my beloved son.

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:17.070
So I'm going to
begin in chapter 42,

00:00:17.070 --> 00:00:19.890
after Joseph has read
all of pharaoh's dreams,

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:23.700
after he's become a
high-ranking official.

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:26.520
And now the brothers are
about to come to him.

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:30.000
This kind of book end
narrative for the Joseph story.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.690
Chapter 42, "And Jacob saw that
there were provisions in Egypt,

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:36.518
and Jacob said to his sons,
'Why are you fearful?'

00:00:36.518 --> 00:00:38.310
And he said, 'Look, I
have heard that there

00:00:38.310 --> 00:00:39.600
are provisions in Egypt.

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:43.380
Go down there, get us provisions
from there that we may live

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:44.820
and not die.'

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:48.810
And the 10 brothers of Joseph
went to buy grain from Egypt.

00:00:48.810 --> 00:00:51.840
But Benjamin, Joseph's
brother, Jacob

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:53.790
did not send with
his brothers, for he

00:00:53.790 --> 00:00:56.550
thought, lest harm befall him."

00:00:56.550 --> 00:00:59.040
Benjamin is now the favored son.

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:01.710
He is the new Joseph
to his brothers.

00:01:01.710 --> 00:01:04.019
You other brothers
go, because there

00:01:04.019 --> 00:01:06.060
could be some harm on the way.

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:10.440
But don't let me lose my
beloved son, the son of Rachel.

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:12.600
"And the sons of Israel
came to buy provisions

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:14.160
among those who
came, for there was

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:16.200
famine in the land of Canaan.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:18.390
As for Joseph, he was
regent of the land,

00:01:18.390 --> 00:01:20.250
he was provider
to all the people.

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:22.470
And Joseph's brothers came
and bowed down to him,

00:01:22.470 --> 00:01:23.820
and their faces to the ground.

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:26.070
And Joseph saw his brothers
and recognized them,

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:29.520
and he played the stranger to
them and spoke harshly to them.

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:32.070
And he says, 'Where
have you come from?'"

00:01:32.070 --> 00:01:34.000
And just notice here
what's going on.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:36.220
Notice they bow
down to the ground.

00:01:36.220 --> 00:01:38.325
And if you remember your
details in the text,

00:01:38.325 --> 00:01:42.930
you know this is specifically
from Joseph's dreams,

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:45.150
when all of the [INAUDIBLE]
bowed down to Joseph.

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:47.940
And now you're going to see
this same image of the bowing

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:50.850
down repeated again
and again and again.

00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:52.950
"And Joseph recognized
his brothers

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:54.960
but they did not recognize him.

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:57.780
And Joseph remembered the dreams
he had dreamed about them.

00:01:57.780 --> 00:01:59.365
And he said to them,
'You are spies!

00:01:59.365 --> 00:02:01.740
To see the land's nakedness
you have come,' And they said

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:04.420
to him, 'No, my lord, for your
servants have come to buy food.

00:02:04.420 --> 00:02:05.730
We are all the sons of one man.

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:06.583
We are honest.

00:02:06.583 --> 00:02:09.000
Your servants would never be
spies.'" And he said to them,

00:02:09.000 --> 00:02:12.030
'No, for the land's nakedness
you have come to see.'

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:15.150
And it's this weird accusation
he makes against them.

00:02:15.150 --> 00:02:16.950
You are spies.

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:19.740
But I want you to think
about what does this

00:02:19.740 --> 00:02:22.740
have to do to the previous
episode that we've seen?

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:24.900
This second part
of the Joseph story

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:26.580
is a playing out
of the first part.

00:02:26.580 --> 00:02:29.190
He needs them to
see their misdeeds.

00:02:29.190 --> 00:02:31.590
He needs them to replay
that drama one more

00:02:31.590 --> 00:02:35.940
time to get them to stop and
to turn back from their ways,

00:02:35.940 --> 00:02:37.600
to see their errors.

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:40.350
So why is he accusing
them of spies?

00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:41.880
I think it's simple enough.

00:02:41.880 --> 00:02:43.620
Is that not what
they accuse Joseph

00:02:43.620 --> 00:02:45.840
of being when his father
would send them out

00:02:45.840 --> 00:02:47.460
to bring ill report?

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:49.320
What is he accusing them of now?

00:02:49.320 --> 00:02:51.600
He's accusing them
of being spies.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:54.390
It's a replay of
that first story.

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:57.390
"12 brothers your servants are,
and we are the sons of one man

00:02:57.390 --> 00:02:59.070
in the land of
Canaan, and, look,

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:02.910
the youngest is now with our
father, and one is no more.'

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:05.340
And Joseph said to them,
"That's just what I told.

00:03:05.340 --> 00:03:06.570
You are spies.

00:03:06.570 --> 00:03:09.480
You shall not leave this place
unless your youngest brother

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:10.260
comes here.

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:12.388
Send one of you to
bring your brother.

00:03:12.388 --> 00:03:14.430
And as for the rest of
you, you will be detained,

00:03:14.430 --> 00:03:16.890
and your words will be tested
as to whether the truth is

00:03:16.890 --> 00:03:17.500
with you.

00:03:17.500 --> 00:03:20.160
And if not, by Pharaoh,
you must be spies.'

00:03:20.160 --> 00:03:22.260
And he put them under
guard for three days.

00:03:22.260 --> 00:03:24.420
And Joseph said to
them on the third day,

00:03:24.420 --> 00:03:26.370
'Do this and live,
for I fear God.

00:03:26.370 --> 00:03:28.800
If you are honest, let
one of your brothers

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:30.510
be detained in this
very guard-house,

00:03:30.510 --> 00:03:32.700
and the rest of you go
forth and bring back

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:35.400
provisions to stave off
the famine in your homes.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:37.590
And your youngest brother
you shall bring to me,

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:41.610
that your words may be
confirmed and you need not die.'

00:03:41.610 --> 00:03:43.620
And they said each to
his brother, 'Alas,

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:46.080
we are guilty for our brother
whose mortal distress we

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:48.390
saw when he pleaded with
us and we did not listen.

00:03:48.390 --> 00:03:50.610
That is why this
distresses overtaken us.'"

00:03:50.610 --> 00:03:52.470
You can see what's
going on here.

00:03:52.470 --> 00:03:53.970
The plan is working.

00:03:53.970 --> 00:03:56.520
The brothers are
recognizing already

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:59.430
the way in which that which
they had done to Joseph

00:03:59.430 --> 00:04:02.110
is coming to bear here.

00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:04.360
"Then Reuben spoke out
to them in these words,

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:06.850
'Didn't I say to you, do
not sin against the boy?

00:04:06.850 --> 00:04:08.260
And you would not listen.

00:04:08.260 --> 00:04:11.780
And now, look, his
blood is requited.'"

00:04:11.780 --> 00:04:13.970
Look it, it's the
same pattern here.

00:04:13.970 --> 00:04:15.740
Remember, the first
story, they all

00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:17.630
speak together with one voice.

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:21.079
Then the first voice that
singles himself out is Reuben.

00:04:21.079 --> 00:04:22.970
It's the same pattern
repeated here.

00:04:22.970 --> 00:04:24.780
They all speak with one voice.

00:04:24.780 --> 00:04:27.110
Then Ruben speaks
out one more time.

00:04:27.110 --> 00:04:31.190
And he even brings out,
"Look, his blood is requited."

00:04:31.190 --> 00:04:35.480
And, of course, Joseph
recognizes all of this

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:37.610
and he weeps.

00:04:37.610 --> 00:04:40.430
And Joseph gives orders that
they fill their bag with grain

00:04:40.430 --> 00:04:42.920
and fill it with silver.

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:45.410
And, of course, when the
brothers discover this,

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:47.480
they're horrified.

00:04:47.480 --> 00:04:49.760
Now they'll be accused
of being spies,

00:04:49.760 --> 00:04:51.860
be accused of being thieves.

00:04:51.860 --> 00:04:54.680
What Joseph is kind of
reminding them of here

00:04:54.680 --> 00:04:59.990
as what he was sold to in
Egypt for-- for that money.

00:04:59.990 --> 00:05:02.510
He's putting the money
right back into their bags

00:05:02.510 --> 00:05:04.430
as this constant reminder.

00:05:04.430 --> 00:05:06.890
And, of course, they report
to their father everything

00:05:06.890 --> 00:05:08.760
that has transpired in Egypt.

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:11.270
How now Simeon is the
one who's left there.

00:05:11.270 --> 00:05:14.120
And in order to get
Simeon back, there, again,

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:15.590
has to be this exchange.

00:05:15.590 --> 00:05:17.150
There has to be a sacrifice.

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:21.920
We must bring back Benjamin
in order to bring back Simeon.

00:05:21.920 --> 00:05:25.760
And Israel's response
is startling.

00:05:25.760 --> 00:05:28.730
"Jacob their father said to
them, 'Me you have bereaved.

00:05:28.730 --> 00:05:31.760
Joseph is no more and
Simeon is no more,

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:33.920
and Benjamin you would take!

00:05:33.920 --> 00:05:36.620
It is I who bear all.'

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:38.630
And Reuben spoke to
his father, saying,

00:05:38.630 --> 00:05:40.910
'My two sons you may
put to death if I do not

00:05:40.910 --> 00:05:42.020
bring him back to you.

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:45.020
Place him in my hands and
I will return him to you.'"

00:05:45.020 --> 00:05:46.520
And here, again,
what do you see?

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:50.330
Reuben working so hard to get
back into his father's graces,

00:05:50.330 --> 00:05:52.147
to really offer up
something absurd.

00:05:52.147 --> 00:05:54.230
Yes, of course, this will
make Israel feel better.

00:05:54.230 --> 00:05:55.605
If you don't bring
him back, he's

00:05:55.605 --> 00:05:57.600
going to kill his two grandsons.

00:05:57.600 --> 00:05:59.090
Reuben's so
desperate to get back

00:05:59.090 --> 00:06:00.770
in his father's
good graces, what

00:06:00.770 --> 00:06:05.570
he's willing to say is, I'll
sacrifice my two sons on behalf

00:06:05.570 --> 00:06:06.590
of Benjamin.

00:06:06.590 --> 00:06:09.810
And, of course, this isn't going
to get anywhere with Israel.

00:06:09.810 --> 00:06:12.260
And he said, "My son shall
not go down with you,

00:06:12.260 --> 00:06:14.133
for his brother is dead."

00:06:14.133 --> 00:06:15.050
And look at this line.

00:06:15.050 --> 00:06:17.300
"And he alone remains."

00:06:17.300 --> 00:06:21.000
And think about all of
the brothers hearing this.

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:22.740
Benjamin alone remains.

00:06:22.740 --> 00:06:25.920
I will not send him with
you, which essentially means,

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:28.200
I'll keep him, and
Simeon's just going

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:30.750
to have to stay there in Egypt.

00:06:30.750 --> 00:06:34.230
Imagine what this is, what these
brothers are witnessing here,

00:06:34.230 --> 00:06:37.010
all on behalf of Benjamin.

00:06:37.010 --> 00:06:39.920
"And should harm befall him
on the way you are going,

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:45.910
you would bring down my gray
head in sorrow to shale."

00:06:45.910 --> 00:06:47.380
It's the same repetition.

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:48.820
He won't be consoled.

00:06:48.820 --> 00:06:53.180
You will bring my head down
to shale in this sorrow.

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:56.290
It's a complete replay
of the Joseph story.

00:06:56.290 --> 00:06:59.140
And, of course, what we need
to anticipate now-- because,

00:06:59.140 --> 00:07:02.740
of course, we know they
will be going back to Egypt.

00:07:02.740 --> 00:07:08.023
And they will be bringing
Benjamin with them.

00:07:08.023 --> 00:07:09.440
SPEAKER 2: Thank
you for watching.

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:11.410
We hope you're enjoying
our Highlight series

00:07:11.410 --> 00:07:14.290
and invite you to explore
all of Hillsdale College's

00:07:14.290 --> 00:07:15.490
online courses.

00:07:15.490 --> 00:07:19.650
They are free and for
everyone who loves to learn.

